  "lines": [
    {
      "who": "LEO",
      "text": "Mia, how can owls turn their heads so far?",
      "board": {
        "type": "title",
        "left": {
          "icon": "🦉",
          "label": "Owl"
        },
        "right": {
          "icon": "🔄",
          "label": "Turn?"
        },
        "mid": "?"
      }
    },
    {
      "who": "MIA",
      "text": "Owls can turn their heads about three-quarters of the way around! That's much farther than you can.",
      "board": {
        "type": "big",
        "icon": "🦉",
        "text": "Three-quarters around!",
        "cue": "three",
        "sub": "Way farther than you",
        "sub_cue": "farther"
      }
    },
    {
      "who": "LEO",
      "text": "Why do they need to?"
    },
    {
      "who": "MIA",
      "text": "Owl eyes are shaped like tubes, so they can't roll them around like we do. Instead, an owl turns its whole head.",
      "punch": "tubes",
      "board": {
        "type": "big",
        "icon": "👀",
        "text": "Eyes can't roll around",
        "cue": "tubes",
        "sub": "So the head turns",
        "sub_cue": "turns"
      }
    },
    {
      "who": "LEO",
      "text": "But how does the neck do that?"
    },
    {
      "who": "MIA",
      "text": "An owl's neck has twice as many bones as yours. More little bones make a bendier, twistier neck!",
      "board": {
        "type": "big",
        "icon": "🦴",
        "text": "Twice the neck bones",
        "cue": "twice",
        "sub": "Bendy and twisty",
        "sub_cue": "bendier"
      }
    },
    {
      "who": "LEO",
      "text": "Doesn't all that twisting hurt?"
    },
    {
      "who": "MIA",
      "text": "No! Special blood vessels in an owl's neck keep blood flowing to its brain, even when it twists.",
      "board": {
        "type": "big",
        "icon": "img:Human_physiology/Servier/capillaries",
        "text": "Blood keeps flowing",
        "cue": "blood",
        "sub": "Even mid-twist!",
        "sub_cue": "twist"
      }
    },
    {
      "who": "LEO",
      "text": "Can I try it?"
    },
    {
      "who": "MIA",
      "text": "Be gentle! Our necks aren't built like that. We move our eyes, and owls move their head.",
      "board": {
        "type": "compare",
        "left": {
          "label": "You",
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "Eyes move",
              "icon": "👀",
              "cue": "eyes"
            },
            {
              "text": "Gentle turns",
              "icon": "🙂",
              "cue": "gentle"
            }
          ]
        },
        "right": {
          "label": "Owl",
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "Head turns",
              "icon": "🦉",
              "cue": "head"
            }
          ]
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "who": "LEO",
      "text": "What else is cool about owls?"
    },
    {
      "who": "MIA",
      "text": "Their super hearing! Many owls can find a mouse in the dark just by listening.",
      "board": {
        "type": "big",
        "icon": "👂",
        "text": "Super hearing",
        "cue": "hearing",
        "sub": "Hunting in the dark",
        "sub_cue": "dark"
      }
    },
    {
      "who": "LEO",
      "text": "Tube eyes, extra neck bones and super hearing. Owls are awesome!",
